# Complexity

For every binary-search step, we scan one complete column to find its maximum.

Finding the maximum in a column takes:

```text
O(m)
```

Binary Search checks:

```text
O(log n)
```

columns.

Therefore:

### Time Complexity

```text
O(m log n)
```

### Space Complexity

```text
O(1)
```

excluding the input matrix.

---

# Key Takeaway

The important trick is:

> **Binary search over columns and find the maximum element in each middle column.**

```text
Choose middle column
        ↓
Find maximum element
        ↓
Compare left and right
        ↓
      /     \
   Larger   Larger
   Left     Right
     ↓         ↓
 Move Left  Move Right
        ↓
    Find Peak
```

Instead of checking every cell in `O(m × n)`, we reduce the search to:

```text
O(m log n)
```

This is a classic example of **Binary Search on a 2D matrix**.
